WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.235
HKDSE 2026, Paper 1, Question 4. Topic: Factorization. This is the full worked solution in English.

2
00:00:10.655 --> 00:00:21.977
Factorize (a) 5x squared y plus 17xy minus 12y, (b) 5x squared y plus 17xy minus 12y minus 10x plus 6.

3
00:00:22.397 --> 00:00:26.924
Step 1. PART (a) — common factor.

4
00:00:27.084 --> 00:00:43.380
Key rule: Common Factor. AB plus AC equals A(B plus C). Every term contains y, so 5x squared y plus 17xy minus 12y equals y(5x squared plus 17x minus 12).

5
00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:54.320
Every term contains y, so take it out: 5x squared y plus 17xy minus 12y equals y(5x squared plus 17x minus 12).

6
00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:59.515
Step 2. PART (a) — split the middle term.

7
00:00:59.675 --> 00:01:14.402
Key rule: Splitting the Middle Term. ac equals minus 60, a plus c equals 17. 20 and minus 3 have product minus 60 and sum 17, giving (5x minus 3)(x plus 4).

8
00:01:14.562 --> 00:01:26.179
For 5x squared plus 17x minus 12: find two numbers with product 5 times (minus 12) equals minus 60 and sum 17, i.e. 20 and minus 3.

9
00:01:26.339 --> 00:01:44.230
5x squared plus 20x minus 3x minus 12 equals 5x(x plus 4)-3(x plus 4) equals (5x minus 3)(x plus 4) therefore 5x squared y plus 17xy minus 12y equals y(5x minus 3)(x.

10
00:01:44.390 --> 00:01:46.262
plus 4).

11
00:01:46.682 --> 00:01:52.247
Step 3. PART (b) — group using part (a).

12
00:01:52.407 --> 00:02:07.798
Group the first three terms (result of (a)) and the last two terms: 5x squared y plus 17xy minus 12y minus 10x plus 6 equals y(5x minus 3)(x plus 4)-2(5x minus 3).

13
00:02:08.218 --> 00:02:13.535
Step 4. PART (b) — common binomial factor.

14
00:02:13.695 --> 00:02:21.892
Both groups contain (5x minus 3): equals (5x minus 3) [y(x plus 4)-2 ].

15
00:02:22.312 --> 00:02:32.514
So the answer is: (a) y(5x minus 3)(x plus 4) (b) (5x minus 3) [y(x plus 4)-2 ].

16
00:02:32.934 --> 00:02:41.742
That completes HKDSE 2026 Paper 1 Question 4. Every step shown here matches the worked solution on the page.
